    {
      "id": "cc8432ef-7ae6-447f-963f-202c468c3666",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Set – properties\r\n\r\nA `Set` stores a group of values with **no duplicates**. It is an **interface** from `java.util`, like `List`.\r\n\r\n**Properties**\r\n- **No duplicates**: adding a value that is already there does nothing (`add` returns `false`).\r\n- **No index**: there is no `get(index)` or `set(index, item)`. You check if a value is in the set with `contains`.\r\n- Order depends on the class you pick:\r\n  - `HashSet` – no fixed order (fastest).\r\n  - `LinkedHashSet` – keeps the **insertion order**.\r\n  - `TreeSet` – keeps the values **sorted**.\r\n- Can only store **objects**, so use `Integer`, `Double`, `Character`… instead of `int`, `double`, `char`.\r\n- `HashSet` and `LinkedHashSet` allow one `null`; `TreeSet` does not allow `null`.\r\n- **Not synchronized** (not thread-safe).\r\n- Very fast `add`, `remove` and `contains` (`HashSet`), much faster than `contains` on a list.",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "cc8432ef-7ae6-447f-963f-202c468c3666"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c5fbd3d7-8739-42ad-aead-64ba3088a7c9",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "//Set \r\n//vlaues insert into set\r\nSet<Integer> arr = new HashSet<Integer>();\r\narr.add(1);\r\narr.add(2);\r\narr.add(3);\r\nSystem.out.println(arr);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 8,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 8,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "[1, 2, 3]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1430c257-fee4-4ba0-bdd2-0dcdfe30e06b",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "//Set \r\n//vlaues insert into set\r\nSet<Integer> arr = new HashSet<Integer>();\r\narr.add(1);\r\narr.add(2);\r\narr.add(3);\r\n\r\narr.addAll(List.of(4, 5, 6));\r\nSystem.out.println(arr);\r\n\r\narr.removeAll(List.of(1, 2));\r\nSystem.out.println(arr);\r\n\r\nboolean containsThree = arr.contains(3);\r\nSystem.out.println(containsThree);\r\n",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 14,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]\r\n[3, 4, 5, 6]\r\ntrue\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 14
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "eb7e0b26-7eba-40ca-8706-ad9ef80dca5b",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "//Syntax\r\n//Set<DataType> variable_name = new HashSet<DataType>();\r\n\r\n//this is to create an empty Set\r\n// Method: new HashSet<>()\r\n// What:   creates an empty set with no fixed order\r\n// Use:    when you need unique values and the order does not matter\r\nSet<String> fruits = new HashSet<String>();\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The set is: \" + fruits);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "eb7e0b26-7eba-40ca-8706-ad9ef80dca5b",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 1,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 1,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "The set is: []\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2e4c6a20-1deb-4c5b-99a7-f0c499461791",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Set<String> fruits = new HashSet<String>();\r\n\r\n//this is to add items to the set\r\n// Method: add(item)\r\n// What:   adds the item if it is not already there; returns true if added, false if it was a duplicate\r\n// Use:    to put new unique values into the set\r\nfruits.add(\"Apple\");\r\nfruits.add(\"Banana\");\r\nfruits.add(\"Mango\");\r\nboolean added = fruits.add(\"Banana\"); // duplicate, not added\r\n\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Was Banana added again? \" + added);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The set is: \" + fruits);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "2e4c6a20-1deb-4c5b-99a7-f0c499461791",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 2,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 2,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Was Banana added again? false\r\nThe set is: [Apple, Mango, Banana]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 2
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dfc8512f-0728-474f-ad26-1577b01fde3c",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Set<String> fruits = new HashSet<>(Set.of(\"Apple\", \"Banana\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to add all items of another collection\r\n// Method: addAll(collection)\r\n// What:   adds every item of the collection, skipping the ones already in the set; returns true if the set changed\r\n// Use:    to add many values at once (also a quick way to remove duplicates from a list)\r\nList<String> more = List.of(\"Mango\", \"Apple\", \"Kiwi\", \"Kiwi\");\r\nfruits.addAll(more);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The set is: \" + fruits);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "dfc8512f-0728-474f-ad26-1577b01fde3c",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 3,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "The set is: [Apple, Kiwi, Mango, Banana]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3317dfe0-84b0-4f06-a142-221177a32bb5",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Set<String> fruits = new HashSet<>(Set.of(\"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Mango\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to remove an item by its value\r\n// Method: remove(item)\r\n// What:   removes the item; returns true if it was there, false if not\r\n// Use:    to take a value out of the set (there is no index, so you remove by value)\r\nboolean removed = fruits.remove(\"Banana\");\r\nboolean removedMissing = fruits.remove(\"Grapes\");\r\n\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Removed Banana? \" + removed);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Removed Grapes? \" + removedMissing);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The set is: \" + fruits);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "3317dfe0-84b0-4f06-a142-221177a32bb5",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 4,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 4,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Removed Banana? true\r\nRemoved Grapes? false\r\nThe set is: [Apple, Mango]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3df2a957-4340-41ff-96c1-e96544241f10",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Set<String> fruits = new HashSet<>(Set.of(\"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Mango\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to check if one item is in the set\r\n// Method: contains(item)\r\n// What:   returns true if the item is in the set\r\n// Use:    to check if a value exists (very fast on a HashSet)\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Has Apple? \" + fruits.contains(\"Apple\"));\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Has Grapes? \" + fruits.contains(\"Grapes\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to check if all items of another collection are in the set\r\n// Method: containsAll(collection)\r\n// What:   returns true only if every item of the collection is in the set\r\n// Use:    to check if one set is a subset of another\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Has Apple and Mango? \" + fruits.containsAll(List.of(\"Apple\", \"Mango\")));\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Has Apple and Kiwi? \" + fruits.containsAll(List.of(\"Apple\", \"Kiwi\")));",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "3df2a957-4340-41ff-96c1-e96544241f10",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 5,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 5,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Has Apple? true\r\nHas Grapes? false\r\nHas Apple and Mango? true\r\nHas Apple and Kiwi? false\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fbd461e6-5b78-4d63-b41b-7b308bce3660",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Set<String> fruits = new HashSet<>(Set.of(\"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Mango\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to get the number of items\r\n// Method: size()\r\n// What:   returns how many items are in the set\r\n// Use:    to know how many unique values you have\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Size: \" + fruits.size());\r\n\r\n// Method: isEmpty()\r\n// What:   returns true if the set has no items\r\n// Use:    to check before working with the set\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Is empty? \" + fruits.isEmpty());",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "fbd461e6-5b78-4d63-b41b-7b308bce3660",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 6,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 6,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Size: 3\r\nIs empty? false\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "137e765d-8199-48d1-90c0-d3234d4a9e8e",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Set<Integer> numbers = new HashSet<>(Set.of(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6));\r\n\r\n//this is to remove every item that is also in another collection\r\n// Method: removeAll(collection)\r\n// What:   removes all items that are in the collection; returns true if the set changed\r\n// Use:    to take many values out at once\r\nnumbers.removeAll(List.of(1, 2));\r\nSystem.out.println(\"After removeAll: \" + numbers);\r\n\r\n//this is to keep only the items that are also in another collection\r\n// Method: retainAll(collection)\r\n// What:   removes every item that is NOT in the collection; returns true if the set changed\r\n// Use:    to keep only the common values\r\nnumbers.retainAll(List.of(3, 4, 10));\r\nSystem.out.println(\"After retainAll: \" + numbers);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "137e765d-8199-48d1-90c0-d3234d4a9e8e",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 7,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 7,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "After removeAll: [3, 4, 5, 6]\r\nAfter retainAll: [3, 4]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "8f41ccf1-3b8e-40de-8c07-ed139e5c0043",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Set<Integer> numbers = new HashSet<>(Set.of(5, 12, 7, 20, 3, 18));\r\n\r\n//this is to remove every item that matches a rule\r\n// Method: removeIf(condition)\r\n// What:   removes all items for which the condition is true\r\n// Use:    to filter the set, here: remove the numbers smaller than 10\r\nnumbers.removeIf(n -> n < 10);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The set is: \" + numbers);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "8f41ccf1-3b8e-40de-8c07-ed139e5c0043",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 8,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 8,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "The set is: [18, 20, 12]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "9ec8d410-d7cd-4661-aabd-f1c65d385c1e",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Set operations – union, intersection, difference\r\n\r\nA set works like a set in maths. The three common operations use the bulk methods above.\r\n`addAll`, `retainAll` and `removeAll` **change** the set, so make a copy first with `new HashSet<>(a)` if you want to keep the original.\r\n\r\n| Operation | Meaning | Method |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Union `A ∪ B` | items in A **or** B | `addAll` |\r\n| Intersection `A ∩ B` | items in A **and** B | `retainAll` |\r\n| Difference `A − B` | items in A but **not** in B | `removeAll` |",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "9ec8d410-d7cd-4661-aabd-f1c65d385c1e"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b6e6a61c-d56b-4605-9106-ad6d9873f578",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Set<Integer> a = new HashSet<>(Set.of(1, 2, 3, 4));\r\nSet<Integer> b = new HashSet<>(Set.of(3, 4, 5, 6));\r\n\r\n//this is to make a copy of a set\r\n// Method: new HashSet<>(collection)\r\n// What:   creates a new set with all items of the collection\r\n// Use:    to work on a copy so the original does not change\r\n\r\n//union: all items of a and b\r\nSet<Integer> union = new HashSet<>(a);\r\n// Method: addAll(collection)\r\n// What:   adds every item of b that is not already in the copy\r\n// Use:    to build the union\r\nunion.addAll(b);\r\n\r\n//intersection: only the items in both\r\nSet<Integer> intersection = new HashSet<>(a);\r\n// Method: retainAll(collection)\r\n// What:   keeps only the items that are also in b\r\n// Use:    to build the intersection\r\nintersection.retainAll(b);\r\n\r\n//difference: items in a but not in b\r\nSet<Integer> difference = new HashSet<>(a);\r\n// Method: removeAll(collection)\r\n// What:   removes every item that is also in b\r\n// Use:    to build the difference\r\ndifference.removeAll(b);\r\n\r\nSystem.out.println(\"a = \" + a + \", b = \" + b);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Union: \" + union);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Intersection: \" + intersection);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Difference (a - b): \" + difference);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "b6e6a61c-d56b-4605-9106-ad6d9873f578",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 9,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 9,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "a = [1, 2, 3, 4], b = [3, 4, 5, 6]\r\nUnion: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]\r\nIntersection: [3, 4]\r\nDifference (a - b): [1, 2]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 9
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "d590b7b5-915f-42cb-9da1-c18f07d26451",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "//this is to create an IMMUTABLE set with Set.of()\r\n// Method: Set.of(items...)\r\n// What:   creates an IMMUTABLE set (cannot add or remove); duplicates in the values cause an error\r\n// Use:    for fixed data that must not change\r\nSet<String> days = Set.of(\"Mon\", \"Tue\", \"Wed\");\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The set is: \" + days);\r\n\r\n//days.add(\"Thu\");                  // not allowed: a Set.of() set cannot be changed (the program stops with an error)\r\n//Set<String> bad = Set.of(\"A\", \"A\"); // not allowed: duplicate values in Set.of() throw an error\r\n\r\n//this is to make an immutable copy of another set\r\n// Method: Set.copyOf(collection)\r\n// What:   creates an IMMUTABLE copy; duplicates are removed\r\n// Use:    to share a set without letting others change it\r\nSet<String> copy = Set.copyOf(List.of(\"Mon\", \"Mon\", \"Fri\"));\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The copy is: \" + copy);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "d590b7b5-915f-42cb-9da1-c18f07d26451",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 10,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 10,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "The set is: [Tue, Mon, Wed]\r\nThe copy is: [Mon, Fri]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "f98d917a-a5ca-4656-aea1-3784d737e5ba",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "List<String> names = new ArrayList<>(List.of(\"Zoya\", \"Jane\", \"Zoya\", \"Doe\", \"Jane\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to remove duplicates from a list by turning it into a set\r\n// Method: new LinkedHashSet<>(collection)\r\n// What:   creates a set from the list; duplicates are dropped and the first-seen order is kept\r\n// Use:    to get the unique values of a list\r\nSet<String> unique = new LinkedHashSet<>(names);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The list is: \" + names);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Unique values: \" + unique);\r\n\r\n//this is to turn the set back into a list\r\n// Method: new ArrayList<>(collection)\r\n// What:   creates a list with all items of the set\r\n// Use:    when you need an index (get) again\r\nList<String> uniqueList = new ArrayList<>(unique);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"First unique name: \" + uniqueList.get(0));\r\n\r\n//this is to convert the set to a normal array\r\n// Method: toArray(new String[0])\r\n// What:   returns a normal array with all items of the set\r\n// Use:    when a method needs an array instead of a set\r\nString[] arr = unique.toArray(new String[0]);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Array length: \" + arr.length);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "f98d917a-a5ca-4656-aea1-3784d737e5ba",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 11,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 11,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "The list is: [Zoya, Jane, Zoya, Doe, Jane]\r\nUnique values: [Zoya, Jane, Doe]\r\nFirst unique name: Zoya\r\nArray length: 3\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 11
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "8721a081-dc53-4e10-ab42-703842a8d62a",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Set<String> fruits = new LinkedHashSet<>(List.of(\"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Mango\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to go through every item (a set has no index, so you cannot use get(i))\r\n// Method: for-each loop  (for (Type item : set))\r\n// What:   gives you each item one by one\r\n// Use:    to read every value of the set\r\nfor (String fruit : fruits) {\r\n    System.out.println(\"Fruit: \" + fruit);\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Method: forEach(action)\r\n// What:   runs the action once for every item\r\n// Use:    a shorter way to do the same with a lambda\r\nfruits.forEach(fruit -> System.out.println(\"Upper: \" + fruit.toUpperCase()));",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "8721a081-dc53-4e10-ab42-703842a8d62a",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 12,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 12,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Fruit: Apple\r\nFruit: Banana\r\nFruit: Mango\r\nUpper: APPLE\r\nUpper: BANANA\r\nUpper: MANGO\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "98fe1c2b-fc2f-47ec-8138-7dd05a880750",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Set<String> a = new HashSet<>(Set.of(\"Apple\", \"Banana\"));\r\nSet<String> b = new LinkedHashSet<>(List.of(\"Banana\", \"Apple\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to compare two sets\r\n// Method: equals(otherSet)\r\n// What:   returns true if both sets have the same items; order and set type do not matter\r\n// Use:    to check if two sets hold the same values\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Are they equal? \" + a.equals(b));\r\nb.add(\"Mango\");\r\nSystem.out.println(\"After adding Mango to b: \" + a.equals(b));",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "98fe1c2b-fc2f-47ec-8138-7dd05a880750",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 13,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 13,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Are they equal? true\r\nAfter adding Mango to b: false\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 13
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "24f50c27-4ac1-4a0f-ad4b-230e03b2a9b6",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Set<String> fruits = new HashSet<>(Set.of(\"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Mango\"));\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Before clear: \" + fruits);\r\n\r\n//this is to remove every item\r\n// Method: clear()\r\n// What:   removes all items; the set becomes empty\r\n// Use:    to reuse the set from scratch\r\nfruits.clear();\r\nSystem.out.println(\"After clear: \" + fruits);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Is empty? \" + fruits.isEmpty());",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "24f50c27-4ac1-4a0f-ad4b-230e03b2a9b6",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 14,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Before clear: [Apple, Mango, Banana]\r\nAfter clear: []\r\nIs empty? true\r\n"
          },
